{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Braem2005-CMS-HF-Al-2xSiO2-Nb2O5",
  "Source": "A. Braem, C. David, and C. Joram, \"Metal multi-dielectric mirror coatings for Cherenkov detectors,\" Nucl. Instrum. Methods Phys. Res. A 553, 182-186 (2005). doi:10.1016/j.nima.2005.08.074 - Sec. 4 p. 184 ('Cr adhesion layer (10 nm)/Al reflectance layer (70 nm)/2 pairs of SiO2/Nb2O5 (66/53 nm)'); Sec. 5 p. 186 and Fig. 6",
  "Notes": "Enhanced-aluminium reflective film for the CMS Hadronic Forward calorimeter air-core light guides: maximum reflectivity at 400-650 nm at about 70 deg incidence, with suppression of the UV below 400 nm; sputtered roll-to-roll on 75 um polyester (Melinex 400)\nSpecification: Sec. 1 p. 183: maximum reflectivity in 400 < lambda < 650 nm for incidence angles of about 70 deg (on average six reflections); suppression of the UV component below 400 nm desired.\nReported: Sec. 5 p. 186 / Fig. 6: measured at 30 deg the film reaches a peak reflectivity of about 98 % at 500 nm. From Fig. 6 (read off the plot, approximate): measured and simulated R at 30 deg ~97-98 % over ~450-600 nm, with a deep minimum (~55 % measured) near 390 nm and a secondary maximum ~90 % near 360 nm; simulated R at 70 deg ~95-96 % over ~400-600 nm, its short-wavelength dip shifted to ~360 nm.\nNotes: The paper lists the stack substrate-up: polyester / Cr 10 nm / Al 70 nm / 2 pairs SiO2/Nb2O5 (66/53 nm); assumed SiO2 on the Al and Nb2O5 outermost (the paper says pairs are written low/high from the metal outward and 'The layer stack terminates usually with a H-layer', Fig. 1), so from the air side: Nb2O5 53 / SiO2 66 / Nb2O5 53 / SiO2 66 / Al. The 70 nm Al film is treated as the opaque substrate (transmission ~1e-4 in the visible), so the Cr layer and polyester are omitted. No optical constants printed; generic SiO2/Nb2O5 database dispersions and measured Al data are used (sputtered films may differ). Fig. 6 measurement at 30 deg, unpolarized; the 70 deg design condition should be compared as the s/p average too. reference_nm 500 is the reported peak, not a stated design wavelength. Four layers, total 238 nm dielectric (2 x 66 + 2 x 53).\nLayers from Sec. 4 p. 184 ('Cr adhesion layer (10 nm)/Al reflectance layer (70 nm)/2 pairs of SiO2/Nb2O5 (66/53 nm)'); Sec. 5 p. 186 and Fig. 6; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours R 98.4 % at 500 nm, 30 deg; paper peak R ~98 % at 500 nm.",
  "Wavelength": [
    400,
    410,
